{"authored" [{"question" "q-282783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix\n  \n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat are the dimensions of ${R}^{T}?$\n\n${R}^{T}$ is a \n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\times $\n{{field-2}}\n matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/state.json" "file_sha256" "b82e265064eb50926e1568a31f87b67cdadcec446ef5a4924658cc53290ef798" "basis" 752 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When a matrix is transposed, its dimensions switch from $m\\times n$ to $n\\times m.$\n\nSo, since $R$ is a $5\\times 2$ matrix, the transpose ${R}^{T}$ is a $2\\times 5$ matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/state.json" "file_sha256" "b82e265064eb50926e1568a31f87b67cdadcec446ef5a4924658cc53290ef798" "basis" 752 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "48e7decd4a6598f288c6775e9dcc29a21d7c37d9fcbf251eb9f4f98a97b403a8" "basis" 752 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282783" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/state.json" "file_sha256" "b82e265064eb50926e1568a31f87b67cdadcec446ef5a4924658cc53290ef798" "basis" 752 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-282783" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/state.json" "file_sha256" "b82e265064eb50926e1568a31f87b67cdadcec446ef5a4924658cc53290ef798" "basis" 752 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $C^T,$ if \n$[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/example-4386.json" "file_sha256" "08995625a93b2d43b33256d2e68fc5b2dbd3731febf8e9bf552ac60837317f9f" "basis" 752 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the transpose, we interchange the rows and columns:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/example-4386.json" "file_sha256" "08995625a93b2d43b33256d2e68fc5b2dbd3731febf8e9bf552ac60837317f9f" "basis" 752 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If\n    ${A} = \n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        5 & -1 & 0 \\\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack,$\nthen what is ${A^T} ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/example-4387.json" "file_sha256" "3466e1b17c648cabcf1fa818baa7a19eaf8871a1b656f7ba8b79510b395f4a5d" "basis" 752 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4387" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the transpose, we interchange the rows and columns. \n\nHere, there is just a single row, so it becomes a single column:\n\n$$\n{A}^T = \n    \t\t\\left\\lbrack\n    \t\t\\matrix {\n    5 \\ \n    -1 \\ \n    0 \\  \n    \t\t}\n    \t\t\\right\\rbrack\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/example-4387.json" "file_sha256" "3466e1b17c648cabcf1fa818baa7a19eaf8871a1b656f7ba8b79510b395f4a5d" "basis" 752 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4388" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix\n    ${B} = \n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\matrix {\n        1 & 2 & 4 & 2\\\n        4 & 4 & 1 & 1\\\n        3 & -3 & 0 & -1\n    }\n    \\right\\rbrack.$\nWhat are the dimensions of ${B}^T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/example-4388.json" "file_sha256" "e2d450311d1947d10c3cd5b8242bcd50867a80e17102e546db7ea1c20ef435bf" "basis" 752 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4388" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "When a matrix is transposed, its dimensions switch from $N \\times M$ to $M \\times N.$\n\nSo, since $B$ is a $3 \\times 4$ matrix, the transpose ${B}^T$ is a $4\\times3$ matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/example-4388.json" "file_sha256" "e2d450311d1947d10c3cd5b8242bcd50867a80e17102e546db7ea1c20ef435bf" "basis" 752 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973224/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-282747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If\n    $S=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]$,\nthen find the transpose of $S.$\n\n  \n\n| ${S}^{T}=$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/state.json" "file_sha256" "941d8326609ace1e047cecc5459b3213f9404d451c93a2cd649cbad5d65f641c"} {"question" "q-282747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the transpose, we interchange the rows and columns:\n\n$$\n{S}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/state.json" "file_sha256" "941d8326609ace1e047cecc5459b3213f9404d451c93a2cd649cbad5d65f641c"} {"question" "q-282747" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "602e90950ee021cc4083a3a0d9d26e557264f075ea2cfb381fb8c39a55fb3184"} {"question" "q-282747" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037542/state.json" "file_sha256" "941d8326609ace1e047cecc5459b3213f9404d451c93a2cd649cbad5d65f641c"} {"question" "q-282747" "f